(7760324, 1285315, 6804, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful entry for this challenge.  It clearly shows YOUR space, and the mess that surrounds the work area when creating todays feed.  The finished product is no doubt a work of art, but the process is messy. Nobody ever gets to see the work or the effort that goes into the candlelight meal at the end of the week.  Here it is, in living color.  This is one of my favorite photos of this really weird challenge. I can relate to the mess and the effort.  I would love to see a photo of the finished meal. Its tough to make a shot like this appeal to the masses.  I do hope this does well in the challenge.  High marks from me.</td>', 'This is a wonderful entry for this challenge.  It clearly shows YOUR space, and the mess that surrounds the work area when creating todays feed.  The finished product is no doubt a work of art, but the process is messy. Nobody ever gets to see the work or the effort that goes into the candlelight meal at the end of the week.  Here it is, in living color.  This is one of my favorite photos of this really weird challenge. I can relate to the mess and the effort.  I would love to see a photo of the finished meal. Its tough to make a shot like this appeal to the masses.  I do hope this does well in the challenge.  High marks from me.', '2023-11-24 01:08:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(7760325, 1285303, 6804, '<td valign="top">This is a very real space in everyones garage cabinets.  The random chaos is perfect for the way I think of this challenge.  My only question would be your choice of a Black and white version of the image.  Black/white is often used to cut down the chaos of color in an image.  I think the color version might have been just a little louder and more chaotic. Its hard to imagine the color image. As a presentation goes, B/W is probably a more attractive presentation.  But as chaos goes, let the colors scream!  I still gave you high marks for a great entry for this challenge.  Good luck!</td>', 'This is a very real space in everyones garage cabinets.  The random chaos is perfect for the way I think of this challenge.  My only question would be your choice of a Black and white version of the image.  Black/white is often used to cut down the chaos of color in an image.  I think the color version might have been just a little louder and more chaotic. Its hard to imagine the color image. As a presentation goes, B/W is probably a more attractive presentation.  But as chaos goes, let the colors scream!  I still gave you high marks for a great entry for this challenge.  Good luck!', '2023-11-24 01:17:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7760329, 1285270, 6804, '<td valign="top">This image just makes me smile. I keep coming back to look at it again. What a wonderful glimpse into your daily chaos.  I see the two culprits on the couch at the far end of the room.  I love the non-vertical walls and door frames.  (It helps add to the chaotic feel of the shot).  High marks from me, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This image just makes me smile. I keep coming back to look at it again. What a wonderful glimpse into your daily chaos.  I see the two culprits on the couch at the far end of the room.  I love the non-vertical walls and door frames.  (It helps add to the chaotic feel of the shot).  High marks from me, good luck in the challenge.', '2023-11-24 01:59:43.000000', NULL, 1),
